Is this a bug? (Mac OS X 10.6.8, R 2.14.0, data.table 1.7.6)

> library(data.table)
data.table 1.7.6  For help type: help("data.table")
> df=data.frame(x=c("a", "a", "b", "b"), y=c("a", "a", "b", "b"))
> df
  x y
1 a a
2 a a
3 b b
4 b b
> unique(df)
  x y
1 a a
3 b b
> dt=as.data.table(df)
> dt
     x y
[1,] a a
[2,] a a
[3,] b b
[4,] b b
> unique(dt)
     x y
[1,] a a
[2,] b b
> setkey(dt, x)
> unique(dt)
Error in `[.default`(x, , key(x), with = FALSE) : 
  incorrect number of dimensions


--Steve


From mdowle at mdowle.plus.com  Thu Dec 15 09:47:13 2011
From: mdowle at mdowle.plus.com (Matthew Dowle)
Date: Thu, 15 Dec 2011 08:47:13 +0000
Subject: [datatable-help] calling unique on data table with a key
